---
title: "Tree-draft Changeset process"
---
%% States are rounded boxes; the diamond is the publish check, not a state.
flowchart LR
    start(( )) -- "new<br>changeset" --> draft
    draft(["draft"]) -- "submission" --> check{"publish<br/>checks"}
    check -- "pass" --> published(["published"])
    draft -- "discard" --> discarded(["discarded"])

    np["Creates a new tree revision.
        Creates new node-versions, updates <em>valid_to_rev</em> of updated nodes' now-previous node-version.
        Tree revisions are frozen and can't be edited."]
    nc["Conflicts are checked:
        <b>base_rev</b> must equal current latest revision.
        <b>Structural:</b> avoid circular lineage, parent nodes must be valid, WoRMS warnings are displayed.
        <b>approver</b> role publishes changes."]
    nx["Kept for the record, with its changes frozen.
        Can't be edited or published."]
    nd["Composed in browser webapp.
        A tree revision draft is a <em>changeset</em>: a sequence of atomic node operations."]


    draft -.- nd
    check -.- nc
    published -.- np
    discarded -.- nx

    classDef state fill:#ede9fe,stroke:#7c3aed
    classDef note fill:#fef9c3,stroke:#a16207,text-align:left
    classDef dot fill:#111,stroke:#111
    class draft,published,discarded state
    class nd,nc,np,nx note
    class start dot
